Trimmed real data (ruling T1) for the Arch databases; synthetic data for CachyOS.

http/core.db, http/extra.db and http/multilib.db hold 42 packages of Arch
Linux's core, extra and multilib sync databases as served by
https://geo.mirror.pkgbuild.com on 2026-09-25 (x86_64). Edits: only the fields
NAME, BASE, VERSION, ARCH, URL, LICENSE, GROUPS, PROVIDES, REPLACES, DEPENDS
and OPTDEPENDS are kept (no packager names, signatures, checksums, sizes or
build dates); web addresses are kept only for organisations' sites; long
dependency and optional-dependency lists are cut to a few entries. The
databases are rebuilt as gzip tars with fixed timestamps, and the Last-Modified
and ETag answers in http/index.json are invented. The package metadata comes
from Arch Linux's PKGBUILDs, published under the 0BSD license (not
re-verified for this fixture).

http/cachyos.db is synthetic (ruling T1): every package named "synth-...",
"...-synth" or "...-synth-bin", and ttf-aster-mono, are invented, as are every
version, license and packager line in that file (the packager lines hold no
address). Real Arch font packages appear only as dependencies, and ttf-hack
once more as a rebuild with an invented version. It imitates
https://mirror.cachyos.org/repo/x86_64/cachyos/cachyos.db, a zstd tar,
including one old-style entry with a separate "depends" file.

snapshot/ is what fetch() writes from http/, and expected.jsonl is parse() of
snapshot/. Rebuild all three with:
uv run python -m tests.collectors.arch_repos.build_fixture
